The naive 3-uniform route fails H: a standard WalkSAT-style restart solver recovered witnesses on most shipping-sized instances. I’m discarding it. The replacement is still the paper’s native object—a 4-uniform hypergraph—but uses three colors and a pairwise-neutral planting mixture. This avoids the paper-adjacent easy exception: 2-color conflict-free 4-uniform instances are just linear equations mod 2. I’m explicitly screening that shortcut and will report the screening and the standard DPLL cost.
apply patch
