The module is now built around inverse generation and the native conflict-free condition. A quick construction check passes all four presets, and every shipping candidate is also screened against the exact GF(2) two-color shortcut. I’m running the full gates now; the main risk is that the stronger domain-propagating DPLL or min-conflicts attack succeeds on any of the eight fixed trials.
